<h2>Deck-wide defaults</h2>

<p>
  <c>defaults</c> in <c>deck.json</c> is a <c><slide></c> block applied to <b>every</b> slide; <c>columns</c> is the same for slides that show two columns and <c>textOnly</c> for slides without code. A slide's own settings win.
</p>

<code lang=jsonc>
  "defaults": {
    "justify": "true",
    "padding": "9vmin 12vmin",
    "heading-size": "56"
  },
  "columns": {
    "valign": "center"
  },
  "textOnly": {
    "halign": "center",
    "valign": "center"
  }
</code>

<p>
  Together with <c>themes</c>, <c>vars</c>, <c>header</c>/<c>footer</c> and <c>css</c> it is enough to build a house style once and
  reuse it for every deck of a school or company.
</p>

<notes>
  Defaults accept any key a slide accepts: layout, theme, background, transition, --variables.
</notes>
